    "q-72038": {
      "dom_id": "step-q72038",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Which of the following is a type I region in two-dimensional space?",
      "worked_solution": "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type I region has the property that a vertical line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type I region is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14252915/assets/af08994008c1df01d052fbc345e6892fed33b7d82ad2de5eb55089e9a879e602.png)",
